  <!-- CLOSING -->
  <h2>The Bigger Picture</h2>
  <div class="divider"></div>

  <p>
    Ashwagandha is not just one herb. It represents something larger &mdash; the validation of an entire system of medicine that was developed through thousands of years of careful observation.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every clinical trial that confirms Ashwagandha's benefits is also confirming the Ayurvedic framework that classified it. When science proves that Ashwagandha reduces cortisol, it validates the Rasayana concept. When it proves neuroprotection, it validates the Medhya classification. When it proves immune modulation, it validates the Ojas theory.
  </p>

  <p>
    The scientists leading this work &mdash; Patwardhan, Tillu, Vaidya, Valiathan &mdash; are not choosing between tradition and science. They are proving that <strong>good science and ancient wisdom can walk the same path.</strong>
  </p>

  <div class="quote">
    <p>"We don't need to discover new drugs from scratch. We need to validate what has already been working for thousands of years."</p>
    <span class="source">&mdash; The reverse pharmacology approach</span>
  </div>

  <p>
    The next time you hold a spoonful of Ashwagandha powder, know this: you're not taking a "supplement." You're taking a 3,000-year-old medicine that has now been validated by the most rigorous tools modern science has to offer. The ancient Vaidyas would smile.
  </p>

